      "message": "One solution to this would be adding `$(location :androidx.core_core-nodeps)` as the jarjar script supports taking in multiple jars. However, This might be a problem in the future incase someone decides to add a new jar to `framework-cronet` but forget to add it to the `jarjar rules`.\n\nI think the best way to do this is do the jarjaring on the implementation module `cronet_aml_java` and have `androidx.core_core-nodeps` as a static lib there. This way we\u0027re sure that everything included in the implementation jar is being jarjared correctly.",
